window.TTBX={"meta":{"title":"Neon Ledger","subtitle":"An expansion for The Technomancer's Textbook","author":"Written for Alex","note":"Original material. Designed against the conventions of fifth edition and the lore of the cyberpunk tabletop tradition \u2014 Cyberpunk 2020/RED's roles and Humanity loss, Shadowrun's Essence, Gibson's ICE, and Altered Carbon's stacks and sleeves \u2014 but written from scratch rather than reproduced from any of them."},"classes":[{"name":"Wirewalker","hit":"d6","primary":["Int"],"saves":["Dex","Int"],"skillCount":3,"skills":["Deception","Insight","Investigation","Perception","Sleight of Hand","Stealth","Technology"],"armor":"Light armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, one-handed firearms","firearms":"Dart gun, machine pistol, pistol \u2014 plus any simple firearm","tools":"Hacking tools, electrician's tools","resource":"Bandwidth","tagline":"Walks into a building through its cabling and out through its bank account.","description":["There is a moment, about a second and a half after the jack seats, when the room you are sitting in stops being the room you are in. The Wirewalker lives for that second and a half. Everything after it is work \u2014 architecture unfolding in front of you floor by floor, ICE circling the edges of your attention like something that has not eaten in a while, and somewhere at the bottom a file worth more than the building.","Wirewalkers are not technicians. A technician fixes the network; a Wirewalker treats it as terrain. They map it, walk it, and leave through a door that did not exist before they got there. The good ones are never detected. The famous ones always are, which is how they became famous, and why so few of them are still breathing.","The body is the weak point and every Wirewalker knows it. While you are in the NET your meat is a slumped shape in a chair with an expensive cable coming out of it, and the crew standing over it is the only reason you will wake up."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Bandwidth","Programs Known","Max Tier"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Interface, Program Suite","3","3","1"],["2nd","+2","Trace Cleaning","4","4","1"],["3rd","+2","Deck Architecture","6","5","2"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","8","6","2"],["5th","+3","Cascade Run","11","7","3"],["6th","+3","Deck Architecture feature","13","8","3"],["7th","+3","Hot Sim","15","9","3"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","17","10","3"],["9th","+4","Ghost Protocol","20","11","4"],["10th","+4","Deck Architecture feature","22","12","4"],["11th","+4","Deep Dive","24","13","4"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","26","14","4"],["13th","+5","Overclock","29","15","5"],["14th","+5","Deck Architecture feature","31","16","5"],["15th","+5","Cold Read","33","16","5"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","35","17","5"],["17th","+6","Deck Architecture feature","38","17","5"],["18th","+6","Total Immersion","40","18","5"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","42","18","5"],["20th","+6","Root Access","45","19","5"]]},"features":[{"name":"Interface","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your deck is jacked to your nervous system, and Intelligence is the ability that moves it. You use Intelligence whenever a program calls for an attack roll or forces a saving throw."},{"type":"ul","items":["Interface attack bonus = your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier","Interface save DC = 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier"]},{"type":"p","text":"You can only reach an architecture you have a physical or wireless path into. Everything a program does happens at the speed of thought \u2014 a full NET run takes seconds of real time, which is why your crew is usually still arguing about the plan when you tell them the door is open."},{"type":"table","title":"Interface","headers":["Your Level","What You Can Reach"],"rows":[["1st","Any system on the same local network, by cable or by standing next to it"],["5th","Any system within 1 mile that is connected to a public network"],["11th","Any system on the continent you can name and route to"],["17th","Any system, anywhere, that has ever touched the NET"]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Program Suite","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know three programs from the program list, and learn more as you level. Running a program costs Bandwidth equal to twice its tier. Your Bandwidth pool is shown on the class table; you regain all of it on a long rest and half of it, rounded down, on a short rest spent jacked out and cooling."},{"type":"p","text":"Whenever you gain a level in this class you can also swap one program you know for another of the same tier or lower \u2014 decks are rewritten between jobs as a matter of hygiene."},{"type":"table","title":"Program List","headers":["Tier","Program","Effect"],"rows":[["1","Ping","You learn the number, rough position and alert state of every node and construct on the floor you occupy."],["1","Sleight","One camera, lock, turnstile or sensor within the architecture obeys one instruction for 1 minute."],["1","Scramble","A construct you can reach has disadvantage on its next attack against you, and cannot report you until the end of your next turn."],["2","Icepick","Make an Interface attack against one ICE. On a hit it takes 3d8 damage and its next action is lost to error handling."],["2","Skim","Copy one file, account or credential you have located. The theft is not noticed until the next audit."],["2","Deadbolt","Seal one physical door, vehicle or weapon's smartlink against its owner for 10 minutes."],["3","Meltdown","One machine, drone or vehicle within the architecture's physical reach takes 6d6 fire damage as you drive its power cell past tolerance."],["3","Wraith","You become invisible to the architecture's logs for 1 hour. Nothing you do this hour can be traced to you afterward."],["3","Puppet Thread","A drone or automated turret under the architecture's control fights for you for 1 minute."],["4","Cascade","Every ICE on your current floor makes a saving throw against your Interface DC. On a failure it is disabled for 1 minute."],["4","Blackout","All powered light, comms and sensors in a 120-foot radius of a node you control fail for 10 minutes."],["4","Rewrite","Alter one record \u2014 a warrant, a debt, a clearance, a death certificate \u2014 convincingly enough to survive casual inspection."],["5","Ghost in the Wire","You leave your body and exist purely as data for up to 1 hour, moving through any connected system at the speed of its cabling. Your body is unconscious and helpless. If it dies while you are out, you have until the end of the hour to find a new host."],["5","Root","You seize an entire architecture. For 1 hour every door, camera, drone and account inside it answers to you, and the corporation that owns it does not yet know."]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Trace Cleaning","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can spend 10 minutes and 2 Bandwidth scrubbing your passage through a system. Any attempt to identify, locate or attribute your intrusion after the fact is made with disadvantage, and automatically fails unless the investigator's passive Intelligence (Technology) equals or exceeds your Interface save DC."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Deck Architecture","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You settle into a way of running. Choose Icebreaker or Wraith Protocol, detailed below. Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each. As normal you can't increase a score above 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Cascade Run","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you run a program of tier 2 or lower, you can immediately run a second program of tier 1 as part of the same action, paying its Bandwidth normally. You can do this a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum once) per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hot Sim","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can run the interface hot, with the safety governors off. While hot, you add your Intelligence modifier to any damage a program deals, and your Interface save DC increases by 2."},{"type":"p","text":"The cost is that feedback reaches you. While hot, any damage dealt to you by ICE is doubled, and you cannot benefit from resistance to it. You can go hot or cold as a bonus action."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ghost Protocol","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your body is no longer a liability while you run. While you are jacked in, you remain aware of your physical surroundings, you can take reactions with your body, and attacks against your body do not have advantage from your condition."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Deep Dive","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can descend past the layer an architecture admits to having. Once per long rest you can spend 10 Bandwidth to reach a system's root layer directly, skipping every intervening floor and every piece of ICE standing on them. What waits at the root is the DM's business, and it is rarely just a file."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Overclock","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action you can push the deck past its rating, gaining 10 temporary Bandwidth that lasts for 1 minute. When the minute ends, you take 4d10 psychic damage and gain one level of exhaustion. You can do this once per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Cold Read","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have run enough architectures to recognise the hand that built one. On first entering an architecture you learn its owner, its rough age, whether it holds black ICE, and one thing its architect was trying to hide \u2014 usually the floor they over-defended."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Total Immersion","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You no longer need a deck. Your nervous system is the deck. You can interface with any system you touch, you cannot be locked out by removing hardware from you, and you have resistance to damage dealt by ICE."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Root Access","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, you can take 1 minute to seize an architecture outright, as though you had run the Root program, without spending Bandwidth and without a check. For the next hour the system is yours: its doors, its drones, its accounts, its cameras, its records."},{"type":"p","text":"Systems you have rooted remember you. You can re-enter any architecture you have ever rooted at will, from anywhere, for as long as it stands."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["wirewalker-icebreaker","wirewalker-wraith-protocol"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Puppeteer","hit":"d8","primary":["Int"],"saves":["Con","Int"],"skillCount":2,"skills":["Athletics","Investigation","Perception","Sleight of Hand","Stealth","Survival","Technology"],"armor":"Light armor, medium armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, martial firearms","firearms":"All simple and martial firearms","tools":"Tinker's tools, electrician's tools, land vehicles","resource":"Uplink","tagline":"Leaves the body in the van and goes to work in something better armoured.","description":["A Puppeteer does not drive. Driving is what you do with your hands. A Puppeteer jumps \u2014 drops their sense of self into a frame of ceramic and servo and wakes up as a four-wheeled thing doing ninety through a service tunnel, or as something the size of a wasp hovering behind a security officer's ear.","The rig makes the distinction between operator and machine an administrative one. Puppeteers describe the switch the way other people describe waking up: not a change of location but a change of what it feels like to have a body. Most of them keep at least one frame running at all times, and a fair number have stopped bothering to specify which body they mean when they say 'I'.","Their weakness is the same as the Wirewalker's and they resent the comparison. While you are out in a frame, the thing you were born in is sitting somewhere with its eyes rolled back. Every Puppeteer has a story about coming home to find someone standing over it."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Uplink","Frames","Frame Tier"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Jump Rig, Frame","2","1","1"],["2nd","+2","Remote Body","3","1","1"],["3rd","+2","Rig Doctrine","3","1","1"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","4","1","1"],["5th","+3","Split Attention","5","2","2"],["6th","+3","Rig Doctrine feature","5","2","2"],["7th","+3","Hardened Uplink","6","2","2"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","7","2","2"],["9th","+4","Field Fabrication","7","2","3"],["10th","+4","Rig Doctrine feature","8","2","3"],["11th","+4","Deep Jump","9","3","3"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","9","3","3"],["13th","+5","Swarm Logic","10","3","4"],["14th","+5","Rig Doctrine feature","11","3","4"],["15th","+5","Redundant Cortex","11","3","4"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","12","3","4"],["17th","+6","Rig Doctrine feature","13","4","5"],["18th","+6","Fleet Command","13","4","5"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","14","4","5"],["20th","+6","Second Body","15","4","5"]]},"features":[{"name":"Jump Rig","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a neural rig that lets you occupy a machine. As an action you can jump into any frame you control within 1 mile. While jumped in:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You see, hear and act through the frame, and your own body is unconscious.","You use your own Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma, and the frame's Strength, Dexterity and Constitution.","You use your own proficiency bonus, saving throw proficiencies and skills.","Damage to the frame does not harm you. If the frame is destroyed while you are in it you are ejected, take 2d6 psychic damage, and cannot jump again until you finish a short rest."]},{"type":"p","text":"You can jump back to your own body as a bonus action, or automatically when your body takes damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Frame","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have built one frame \u2014 a drone, a crawler, a rotor, a wheeled chassis, whatever the job wanted. It uses the Puppeteer Frame statistics, scaled by its tier on the class table. Building a replacement takes 8 hours and 500\u20b5 per tier."},{"type":"table","title":"Puppeteer Frame","headers":["Tier","AC","Hit Points","Speed","Str/Dex/Con","Attack"],"rows":[["1","13","10 + 5 per Puppeteer level","40 ft.","12 / 14 / 12","+Int, 1d8"],["2","15","15 + 6 per Puppeteer level","40 ft.","14 / 16 / 14","+Int, 1d10"],["3","17","20 + 7 per Puppeteer level","50 ft.","16 / 18 / 16","+Int, 2d6"],["4","18","25 + 8 per Puppeteer level","50 ft.","18 / 18 / 18","+Int, 2d8"],["5","20","30 + 9 per Puppeteer level","60 ft.","20 / 20 / 20","+Int, 2d10"]]},{"type":"p","text":"A frame is a construct. It is immune to poison and psychic damage, does not breathe, eat or sleep, and is vulnerable to the effects of EMP. You can spend Uplink to give a frame extra capability \u2014 see Remote Body."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Remote Body","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a pool of Uplink shown on the class table, regained on a long rest. While jumped in, you can spend Uplink as a bonus action for one of the following:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Burn (1) \u2014 the frame's speed doubles until the end of your turn.","Harden (1) \u2014 the frame gains resistance to all damage until the start of your next turn.","Overclock Servos (2) \u2014 the frame makes one extra attack this turn.","Sensor Sweep (1) \u2014 the frame detects every powered object and living creature within 120 feet, through walls.","Emergency Eject (2) \u2014 when the frame would be destroyed, it instead drops to 1 hit point and you are not ejected."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Rig Doctrine","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Swarm Handler or Panzer Jockey. Your doctrine grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Split Attention","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can control a second frame. While jumped in, you can command your other frames with a bonus action; they act on your initiative and can each take one action. Only the frame you are jumped into uses your full ability scores and proficiency \u2014 the others act with their own statistics."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hardened Uplink","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your connection cannot be casually severed. You have advantage on saving throws against effects that would eject you from a frame, jamming has no effect on your control, and your jump range increases to 10 miles."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Field Fabrication","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can build or rebuild a frame in 1 hour instead of 8 using scavenged material, and you can repair a destroyed frame for half the cost of a new one. Over a long rest you can also reconfigure a frame's chassis entirely, changing its shape, movement type and attack."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Deep Jump","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can jump into machines you did not build. As an action you can attempt to seize any vehicle, drone or construct you can see: it makes a Charisma saving throw against your Uplink DC (8 + proficiency + Intelligence), and on a failure you control it as a frame for 10 minutes. Unattended and unintelligent machines fail automatically."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Swarm Logic","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your frames coordinate without you. Frames you are not jumped into now act on their own initiative, take full turns, and add your Intelligence modifier to their attack and damage rolls."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Redundant Cortex","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your sense of self is backed up across every frame you run. You no longer take psychic damage when a frame is destroyed, and if your own body is killed while you are jumped in, you continue to exist in the frame indefinitely \u2014 your mind simply does not come back to a corpse."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Fleet Command","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can control any number of frames within range, and as an action you can give all of them the same order, which each carries out on your initiative."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Second Body","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"One frame becomes indistinguishable from you in every way that matters. Choose a frame: it gains your Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma scores permanently, acts with your full proficiency whether or not you are jumped in, and can act independently while you occupy another frame."},{"type":"p","text":"If your original body dies, you wake up in this one, and the transition is so smooth that you may not notice for some hours which of you is doing the noticing."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["puppeteer-swarm-handler","puppeteer-panzer-jockey"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Chromehound","hit":"d10","primary":["Str","Dex"],"saves":["Str","Con"],"skillCount":2,"skills":["Acrobatics","Athletics","Intimidation","Investigation","Perception","Stealth","Survival"],"armor":"All armor, shields","weapons":"Simple weapons, martial weapons","firearms":"All simple and martial firearms, plus heavy weapons","tools":"One set of artisan's tools of your choice","resource":"Adrenaline","tagline":"Traded most of a person for the reflexes to survive the trade.","description":["Every Chromehound started as someone who decided their body was not adequate to the problem in front of it. The first implant is always practical \u2014 a hand that doesn't shake, an eye that ranges. The tenth is practical too, and by then the arithmetic has stopped being about capability and started being about how much of the original owner is still on the premises.","They are the best close-quarters operators the city produces, and the shortest-lived. Corporations retain them and quietly budget for replacement. Crews want one on the team and want them sitting where they can be seen. The Chromehound knows all of this and takes the work anyway, because the work is the only place the wiring makes sense.","This class is built to be played against the Humanity track. A Chromehound gets stronger as they hollow out, and the strongest ones are perhaps four bad decisions from becoming something the rest of the party has to put down."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Adrenaline","Die","Tolerance"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Combat Awareness, Chrome Tolerance","2","d6","5"],["2nd","+2","Adrenaline Surge","2","d6","5"],["3rd","+2","Combat Doctrine","3","d6","10"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","3","d6","10"],["5th","+3","Extra Attack","3","d8","10"],["6th","+3","Combat Doctrine feature","4","d8","15"],["7th","+3","Threat Assessment","4","d8","15"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","4","d8","15"],["9th","+4","Pain Editor","5","d8","20"],["10th","+4","Combat Doctrine feature","5","d10","20"],["11th","+4","Extra Attack (2)","5","d10","20"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","5","d10","20"],["13th","+5","Hardware Sync","6","d10","25"],["14th","+5","Combat Doctrine feature","6","d10","25"],["15th","+5","Nothing Left to Lose","6","d10","25"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","6","d10","25"],["17th","+6","Combat Doctrine feature","6","d10","25"],["18th","+6","Last Stand","7","d12","30"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","7","d12","30"],["20th","+6","Apex Predator","8","d12","40"]]},"features":[{"name":"Combat Awareness","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your wiring runs threat assessment below the level of thought. You add your Constitution modifier to initiative rolls, you cannot be surprised while conscious, and you always know the direction of the nearest hostile creature within 60 feet."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Chrome Tolerance","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your nervous system has been rebuilt to carry load that would break a civilian. You gain a tolerance buffer equal to the Tolerance column of the class table. The buffer is spent last: your Humanity falls exactly as it would for anyone else, and you pass through Dissociated, Fraying and Flatlining on the same schedule \u2014 but once your Humanity reaches zero, the buffer keeps you on your feet until it too is gone."},{"type":"p","text":"In plain terms: you can carry more chrome than anyone else before the wheels come off. This is not a kindness. It means you will be the one still standing when you should have stopped."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Adrenaline Surge","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a pool of Adrenaline dice shown on the class table, regained on a short or long rest. You can spend them as follows:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Burst. When you make an attack roll, ability check or saving throw, spend one die after seeing the roll and add it to the result.","Sync. As a bonus action, spend one die and add it to your speed in feet times two, and to your AC until the start of your next turn.","Clot. As a bonus action, spend one die and regain hit points equal to the roll plus your Constitution modifier."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Combat Doctrine","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Reflex Arsenal or Bulwark Protocol. Your doctrine grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Extra Attack","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can attack twice, rather than once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Threat Assessment","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As a bonus action you can designate one creature you can see as a threat. Until the end of your next turn you have advantage on attack rolls against it, and it has disadvantage on attack rolls against anyone but you. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Pain Editor","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your implants filter what reaches you. You have resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage while you are below half your hit point maximum, and you are immune to the frightened condition."},{"type":"p","text":"You also no longer notice injury in time to be sensible about it. You do not know your own hit point total; the DM tracks it, and tells you only when you are reduced to 0."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Extra Attack (2)","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can attack three times whenever you take the Attack action on your turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hardware Sync","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Every piece of cyberware you carry is now driven from the same tuned controller. For each 25 Humanity you have spent on installed ware, you gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with weapons, to a maximum of +3."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Nothing Left to Lose","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The emptier you are, the harder you are to stop. While your Humanity is at or below 39% of your starting score, you have advantage on all attack rolls and immunity to the charmed condition."},{"type":"p","text":"While your Humanity is at or below 19%, you also do not die at 0 hit points: you drop to 1 instead, once per long rest. The thing that stands back up is increasingly difficult for the people who knew you to talk to."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Last Stand","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you are reduced to 0 hit points, you can choose to keep acting. For 1 minute you act normally with 0 hit points, cannot be reduced below 0, and cannot be killed. At the end of the minute you drop, unconscious and dying, unless you have been healed above 0. Once per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Apex Predator","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Strength and Dexterity scores increase by 4, to a maximum of 24. You have advantage on initiative, and on the first round of any combat you can take an additional action."},{"type":"p","text":"Your tolerance buffer increases by a further 40 \u2014 you are, at this point, more installed equipment than person, and the equipment is exceptional."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["chromehound-reflex-arsenal","chromehound-bulwark-protocol"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Streetdoc","hit":"d8","primary":["Wis"],"saves":["Int","Wis"],"skillCount":3,"skills":["Deception","Insight","Investigation","Medicine","Nature","Perception","Persuasion","Technology"],"armor":"Light armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, one-handed firearms","firearms":"Dart gun, machine pistol, pistol, revolver","tools":"Herbalism kit, tinker's tools, one type of artisan's tools","resource":"Trauma Dice","tagline":"Keeps people alive in rooms that were not designed for it.","description":["There is a tier of medicine below the hospitals and above the vending machine that sells antibiotics, and the Streetdoc owns it. A back room with good light. A table that has been bleached more times than it has been replaced. A practitioner who will not ask where the bullet came from and will not file anything anywhere.","Some of them trained properly and lost the licence. Some never trained at all and are better than the ones who did. All of them do three jobs that the legitimate system refuses to: they patch trauma without paperwork, they install chrome that has not been approved by anyone, and they pull people back from the far end of the Humanity track when nobody else will take the appointment.","A Streetdoc in a crew is the difference between a hard job and a funeral. They know it. They charge accordingly, and most of them still end up working for free more often than not, which is the quiet tragedy of the profession."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Trauma Dice","Die","Ampules"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Trauma Kit, Field Medicine","4","d6","2"],["2nd","+2","Chem Cook","5","d6","2"],["3rd","+2","Practice","6","d6","3"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","7","d6","3"],["5th","+3","Combat Triage","8","d8","3"],["6th","+3","Practice feature","9","d8","4"],["7th","+3","Counsellor's Licence","10","d8","4"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","11","d8","4"],["9th","+4","Hardline Stabilise","12","d8","5"],["10th","+4","Practice feature","13","d10","5"],["11th","+4","Transplant","14","d10","5"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","15","d10","5"],["13th","+5","Adrenal Override","16","d10","6"],["14th","+5","Practice feature","17","d10","6"],["15th","+5","Crash Cart","18","d10","6"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","19","d10","6"],["17th","+6","Practice feature","20","d10","6"],["18th","+6","Miracle Worker","21","d12","7"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","22","d12","7"],["20th","+6","Death Is Negotiable","24","d12","8"]]},"features":[{"name":"Trauma Kit","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a pool of Trauma Dice shown on the class table, regained on a long rest. As an action, or as a bonus action on a creature you are already touching, you can spend any number of them: the target regains hit points equal to the total rolled plus your Wisdom modifier."},{"type":"p","text":"Trauma Dice are not magic. They work on the living, they do not regrow what is gone, and a creature that has been dead for more than a minute is beyond them."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Field Medicine","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can stabilise a dying creature as a bonus action. When you do, it regains 1 hit point instead of merely stabilising, if you spend at least one Trauma Die."},{"type":"p","text":"You also always know a creature's exact hit point total, conditions, and the nature of any poison, disease, drug or implant affecting it, simply by looking at it for 6 seconds."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Chem Cook","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over a long rest you can prepare a number of ampules shown on the class table, using a herbalism kit or artisan's tools. An ampule can be administered to a willing creature as an action, or thrown up to 20 feet as an improvised weapon. Choose each ampule's type when you prepare it:"},{"type":"table","title":"Ampules","headers":["Ampule","Effect"],"rows":[["Stim","The target gains advantage on attack rolls and saving throws for 1 minute, then one level of exhaustion."],["Coag","The target regains 2d8 + your Wisdom modifier hit points and stops bleeding."],["Clarity","The target ends one effect causing it to be charmed, frightened or poisoned, and has advantage on Wisdom saves for 10 minutes."],["Downer","A creature within 20 feet makes a Constitution saving throw against your Medicine DC or is poisoned for 1 minute; on a failure by 5 or more it also falls unconscious for 1 minute."],["Burnout","The target's next weapon attack this turn deals an extra 3d6 damage, and the target takes 1d6 necrotic damage it cannot reduce."],["Scrub","The target is cured of one disease, one poison, or one drug's addiction progress."]]},{"type":"p","text":"Your Medicine DC is 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier. Unused ampules spoil when you next prepare a batch."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Practice","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Ripperdoc or Trauma Team. Your practice grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Combat Triage","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When an ally within 30 feet of you drops to 0 hit points, you can use your reaction to spend one Trauma Die and bring them to 1 hit point, plus the die roll. You can do this a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Counsellor's Licence","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You are one of the few practitioners willing to treat Humanity loss, and one of the fewer who is any good at it. Therapy you administer costs half the usual credits and restores 2 Humanity per day instead of 1."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, you can spend 10 minutes and one Trauma Die talking a creature down from a Fraying or Flatlining episode: it is treated as one Humanity state higher until its next long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hardline Stabilise","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Allies within 30 feet of you that you can see have advantage on death saving throws, and a creature you have treated within the last hour cannot be reduced below 1 hit point by a source of damage that is not a critical hit."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Transplant","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Over a short rest you can perform surgery to install, remove or replace one piece of cyberware or one augment, without a clinic and without the usual surgery fee."},{"type":"p","text":"Ware you install personally costs 1 less Humanity, to a minimum of 1."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Adrenal Override","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action you can override a creature's endocrine system. Until the end of its next turn it can take an additional action, moves at double speed, and automatically succeeds on Constitution saving throws. It then takes 4d8 necrotic damage and gains one level of exhaustion. Once per creature per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Crash Cart","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can bring back a creature that has been dead for up to 1 minute, provided its body is largely intact. It returns with 1 hit point, one level of exhaustion, and a permanent reduction of 5 to its Humanity maximum \u2014 something is always left behind on the table. Once per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Miracle Worker","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Trauma Dice heal for their maximum value instead of being rolled."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Death Is Negotiable","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, you can spend 1 minute and your entire remaining pool of Trauma Dice on a creature that has been dead for no more than 24 hours. It returns to life with full hit points, all conditions and diseases ended, and any missing limbs replaced with chrome of your choosing."},{"type":"p","text":"The creature's Humanity maximum is permanently reduced by 10. It does not remember being dead. Everyone it knows will notice that it is, in some small way that nobody can name, not quite the same person."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["streetdoc-ripperdoc","streetdoc-trauma-team"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Fixer","hit":"d8","primary":["Cha"],"saves":["Dex","Cha"],"skillCount":4,"skills":["Deception","History","Insight","Intimidation","Investigation","Perception","Performance","Persuasion","Sleight of Hand","Stealth","Technology"],"armor":"Light armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, one-handed firearms","firearms":"Machine pistol, magnum, pistol, revolver","tools":"Forgery kit, one gaming set, one type of artisan's tools","resource":"Favours","tagline":"Does not own the city, but knows who does and what they want.","description":["The Fixer is the reason the job exists. Somebody wanted something, somebody else could get it, and between those two people stood a third who knew them both and took a cut for the introduction. Multiply that by a career and you have a person who can produce a military-grade weapon, a surgeon, a clean identity or a helicopter, given four hours and a reason.","Fixers are not powerful in the way a Chromehound is powerful. Nothing about them wins a firefight. What they have is a map of obligation \u2014 who owes whom, who is overextended this month, whose brother works security at the building you need to enter \u2014 and the nerve to spend that map down to the last favour when it matters.","The job has a half-life. A Fixer survives by being more useful alive than dead to everyone who might otherwise consider the alternative, and that calculation has to be re-run every single week."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Favours","Die","Contacts"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Contacts, Favours","2","d6","2"],["2nd","+2","Market Sense","3","d6","2"],["3rd","+2","Operation","3","d6","3"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","4","d6","3"],["5th","+3","Leverage","4","d8","4"],["6th","+3","Operation feature","5","d8","4"],["7th","+3","Everybody Owes Somebody","5","d8","5"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","6","d8","5"],["9th","+4","Off the Books","6","d8","6"],["10th","+4","Operation feature","7","d10","6"],["11th","+4","The Right Person","7","d10","7"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","8","d10","7"],["13th","+5","Insurance","8","d10","8"],["14th","+5","Operation feature","9","d10","8"],["15th","+5","Untouchable","9","d10","9"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","10","d10","9"],["17th","+6","Operation feature","10","d10","10"],["18th","+6","City in the Pocket","11","d12","10"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","11","d12","12"],["20th","+6","The Whole Board","12","d12","15"]]},"features":[{"name":"Contacts","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know people. You have a number of contacts shown on the class table. Each is a named NPC with a speciality, a personality and a price, created with the DM. When you gain a contact you decide their field: ware, weapons, transport, documents, medicine, information, muscle, access, or law."},{"type":"p","text":"A contact can be reached in minutes and will tell you what they know for free. Anything more costs a Favour, money, or something they want. Contacts are people, not a resource pool: they can be arrested, bought, killed or turned, and a Fixer who burns them carelessly will find the next one harder to make."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Favours","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You carry a ledger of outstanding obligation, represented by Favour dice shown on the class table. You regain all of them when you finish a long rest in a place where you can make calls. Spend them as follows:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Call It In. As an action, spend a die to have a contact deliver something to your location within the hour \u2014 a weapon, a vehicle, a document, a person. The die roll times 1,000\u20b5 is the value ceiling of what arrives.","Name Drop. When you make a Charisma check, spend a die after rolling and add it to the result.","I Know a Guy. When the party needs a specialist, spend a die: one exists, nearby, and will hear you out.","Word Is Out. Spend a die to learn one useful, true piece of information about a person, building or organisation in the city."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Market Sense","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You always know the fair street price of any item, service or person, whether it is available in this city, and roughly who is holding it. You buy at 20% below market and sell at 20% above."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Operation","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Broker or Handler. Your operation grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Leverage","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can spend 10 minutes researching a creature you have met to find the thing it does not want known. The DM tells you one genuine piece of leverage. Once per long rest, you can use it: the creature has disadvantage on saving throws against your Charisma checks for the next hour, and will not willingly raise an alarm about you during that time."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Everybody Owes Somebody","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you fail a Charisma check against a creature, you can spend a Favour die to discover that you have a mutual acquaintance. Reroll the check with advantage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Off the Books","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You and up to eight creatures you name do not appear in official records for the next week: no transaction logs, no biometric hits, no arrival records. Renewing this takes 1 hour and a Favour die."}],"sub":false},{"name":"The Right Person","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can declare that one of your contacts happens to be exactly who you need \u2014 present, positioned, or already inside. The DM adjudicates the details, but the coincidence holds."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Insurance","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have arranged for what happens if this goes badly. When you or an ally within 60 feet would drop to 0 hit points, you can use your reaction and spend two Favour dice: a prearranged contingency fires \u2014 a diversion, an extraction vehicle, a bribed guard looking elsewhere \u2014 and the target drops to 1 hit point and can immediately move up to their speed."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Untouchable","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Too many important people need you alive. Organisations that would otherwise move against you hesitate: you have advantage on saving throws against being charmed, frightened or imprisoned, and any faction that harms you must first weigh the cost, which the DM should make visible in play as delays, warnings and second thoughts."}],"sub":false},{"name":"City in the Pocket","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Favour dice are regained on a short rest as well as a long one, and Call It In has no value ceiling \u2014 if it exists in this city, it can be at your door within the hour, though the price may be dreadful."}],"sub":false},{"name":"The Whole Board","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You see the shape of it all. Once per long rest you can spend 1 minute to ask the DM three questions about any ongoing situation \u2014 who benefits, who is lying, what happens next \u2014 and receive truthful answers."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, each of your contacts has by now become someone: a gang boss, a department head, a chief of staff. One of them, once per long rest, will do something genuinely enormous for you, and afterwards you will owe them, which is how this has always worked."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["fixer-broker","fixer-handler"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Firebrand","hit":"d8","primary":["Cha"],"saves":["Con","Cha"],"skillCount":3,"skills":["Athletics","Deception","History","Insight","Intimidation","Performance","Persuasion","Technology"],"armor":"Light armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, one-handed firearms","firearms":"Machine pistol, micro SMG, pistol","tools":"Two musical instruments, one type of artisan's tools","resource":"Signal","tagline":"Turns an audience into a weather system and stands in the middle of it.","description":["Every authoritarian structure in this setting is terrified of exactly one thing, and it is not guns. It is a crowd that has stopped being afraid. The Firebrand is the person who makes that happen \u2014 on a stage, on a rooftop, on a hijacked frequency at three in the morning, in a square where the drones are already circling.","Some of them are musicians. Some are preachers, comedians, streamers, union organisers or professional liars. The common thread is a voice that people repeat afterwards, and the willingness to stand somewhere visible while saying something expensive.","Firebrands do not live quietly and mostly do not live long. They are also, more often than any other profession in this book, the reason anything in the city ever changes."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Signal","Inspiration Die","Audience"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Stage Presence, Signal","2","d6","30 ft."],["2nd","+2","Crowd Work","3","d6","30 ft."],["3rd","+2","Act","4","d6","30 ft."],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","5","d6","30 ft."],["5th","+3","Anthem","6","d8","60 ft."],["6th","+3","Act feature","7","d8","60 ft."],["7th","+3","Viral","8","d8","60 ft."],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","9","d8","60 ft."],["9th","+4","Feedback","10","d8","120 ft."],["10th","+4","Act feature","11","d10","120 ft."],["11th","+4","Mass Movement","12","d10","120 ft."],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","13","d10","120 ft."],["13th","+5","Martyr's Odds","14","d10","120 ft."],["14th","+5","Act feature","15","d10","120 ft."],["15th","+5","Living Symbol","16","d10","120 ft."],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","17","d10","120 ft."],["17th","+6","Act feature","18","d10","1 mile"],["18th","+6","Riot","19","d12","1 mile"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","20","d12","1 mile"],["20th","+6","Voice of the City","22","d12","City"]]},"features":[{"name":"Stage Presence","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You are always, in some measure, performing, and people respond to it. You add your Charisma modifier to initiative rolls, and you can use Charisma in place of Strength or Dexterity for any check made to be seen, heard, reached or followed by a crowd."},{"type":"p","text":"Your Signal DC is 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Signal","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a pool of Signal shown on the class table, regained on a long rest \u2014 the measure of how much attention you currently command. Spend it as follows:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Hook (1). As a bonus action, one creature within your Audience range that can see or hear you must succeed on a Wisdom save against your Signal DC or have disadvantage on attacks against anyone but you until the end of your next turn.","Lift (1). As a bonus action, an ally within Audience range rolls your Inspiration die and adds it to their next attack roll, check or save.","Drown Out (2). As a reaction when a creature within range speaks, transmits or casts a spell with a verbal component, it must succeed on a Charisma save or the attempt fails and is wasted.","Turn (3). As an action, up to three creatures within range make Wisdom saves or are charmed by you for 1 minute, believing whatever you are currently claiming."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Crowd Work","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can read a group the way others read a person. After 1 minute observing any gathering, you learn its mood, what it wants, what it is afraid of, and what single sentence would move it fastest in a direction of your choosing."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Act","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Agitator or Pirate Signal. Your act grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Anthem","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action you can begin an anthem, sustained with your concentration for up to 1 minute. While it lasts, allies within your Audience range have advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened, and add your Inspiration die to the first attack roll they make on each of their turns."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Viral","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Anything you perform, say or transmit propagates on its own. A message you release reaches the whole city within 24 hours and cannot be fully suppressed. You have advantage on Charisma checks made against any creature that has heard of you \u2014 and by now, most of them have."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Feedback","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature within your Audience range damages you, every hostile creature within 30 feet of it takes thunder damage equal to your Inspiration die + your Charisma modifier as the crowd turns. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Mass Movement","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Turn option can now target any number of creatures within your Audience range, and lasts 10 minutes. Creatures that fail by 5 or more will actively assist you for the duration \u2014 carrying, blocking, shouting, standing in the way of things."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Martyr's Odds","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The story protects you as long as there is someone to tell it. While at least one creature within your Audience range can see you, you have advantage on death saving throws, and when you drop to 0 hit points every ally who can see you gains temporary hit points equal to your Firebrand level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Living Symbol","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have become shorthand for an idea. Creatures who oppose that idea have disadvantage on saving throws against your Signal options; creatures who share it automatically succeed on saves against being frightened while they can see you."},{"type":"p","text":"Your face is on walls you have never visited. This is not entirely an advantage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Riot","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can ignite a crowd. Every creature within your Audience range that is not your ally makes a Wisdom saving throw against your Signal DC. On a failure, for 1 minute it attacks the nearest creature it perceives as an authority, or flees if none is present. Structures, vehicles and cameras in the area are destroyed at the DM's discretion, because that is what happens."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Voice of the City","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Audience range is the city you are in. You can be heard, at will, by every person in it who is near any speaker, screen or open window."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can make a demand of the city. Every creature in it that can hear you makes a Wisdom saving throw against your Signal DC; those that fail spend the next hour doing what you asked, to the best of their ability. Whether the city forgives you afterward is the campaign's problem, not this feature's."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["firebrand-agitator","firebrand-pirate-signal"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Stackborn","hit":"d8","primary":["Con"],"saves":["Wis","Cha"],"skillCount":3,"skills":["Acrobatics","Athletics","Deception","History","Insight","Investigation","Perception","Persuasion","Sleight of Hand","Stealth"],"armor":"Light armor, medium armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, martial firearms","firearms":"All simple and martial firearms","tools":"One type of artisan's tools, one gaming set","resource":"Stack Charge","tagline":"Has died before. Found it survivable. Kept the receipts.","description":["At the top of your spine, seated against the first vertebra, is a cylinder of alloy about the size of a coin. Everything you are is written on it \u2014 the body around it is hardware. You have worn this one for a while. You have worn others. When somebody shoots you in the chest, that is an inconvenience and an expense. When somebody shoots you in the back of the neck, that is murder.","Stackborn come from wherever stacks are cheap enough to be issued and expensive enough to be worth stealing. Some were born to it and have never known a life that ended permanently. Some had it fitted against their will. Some are carrying a stack that used to belong to someone else and have not told anyone, including, on bad nights, themselves.","The class is built around a single question the rest of the table will eventually ask out loud: after the fourth body, is the person sitting there still the one who started the campaign? The Stackborn's answer is usually yes, delivered slightly too quickly."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Charge","Imprints","Needlecast"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Cortical Stack, Sleeve","1","1","\u2014"],["2nd","+2","Muscle Memory","2","1","\u2014"],["3rd","+2","Stack Protocol","2","2","\u2014"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","3","2","\u2014"],["5th","+3","Needlecast","3","2","1 mile"],["6th","+3","Stack Protocol feature","4","3","1 mile"],["7th","+3","Past Lives","4","3","1 mile"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","5","3","1 mile"],["9th","+4","Resleeve","5","4","10 miles"],["10th","+4","Stack Protocol feature","6","4","10 miles"],["11th","+4","Ghostwalk","6","4","10 miles"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","7","5","10 miles"],["13th","+5","Backup","7","5","Planet"],["14th","+5","Stack Protocol feature","8","5","Planet"],["15th","+5","Two Places at Once","8","6","Planet"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","9","6","Planet"],["17th","+6","Stack Protocol feature","9","6","Planet"],["18th","+6","Stack Hardening","10","7","Planet"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","10","7","Planet"],["20th","+6","Real Death","12","8","Anywhere"]]},"features":[{"name":"Cortical Stack","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You carry a cortical stack at the base of your skull. It records you continuously. While it is intact, dying is not final:"},{"type":"ul","items":["When you are reduced to 0 hit points and die, your stack survives unless the killing blow specifically targeted the back of your neck, or the damage was enough to destroy your body entirely.","A surviving stack can be recovered and fitted into a new body \u2014 a sleeve \u2014 in 24 hours, given a clinic and 25,000\u20b5. You return with all your levels, your memories up to the moment of death, and someone else's hands.","If your stack is destroyed, you are dead. Permanently, and beyond any resurrection this book or its parent system can offer."]},{"type":"p","text":"Your stack is an object with AC 20 and 10 hit points, and it can only be attacked by a creature that has you grappled or incapacitated, or by a called shot the DM allows."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Sleeve","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your current body is equipment. When you take a new sleeve, choose one sleeve package: its bonuses replace those of your previous sleeve. You can also swap packages when you gain a level in this class, representing a refit."},{"type":"table","title":"Sleeve Packages","headers":["Package","Benefit"],"rows":[["Combat","+2 Strength or Dexterity (max 22). You gain proficiency with martial weapons."],["Endurance","+2 Constitution (max 22). Your hit point maximum increases by your Stackborn level."],["Infiltration","+2 Dexterity (max 22). You gain proficiency in Stealth and can squeeze through any gap a cat could."],["Diplomatic","+2 Charisma (max 22). You gain proficiency in Persuasion and one language."],["Labour","+2 Strength (max 22). Your carrying capacity doubles and you ignore the massive property on firearms."],["Synthetic","You do not need to eat, drink or breathe, and you have advantage on saving throws against poison and disease. Healing you receive is halved."]]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Muscle Memory","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Something of every body you have worn stays with you. You have a number of imprints shown on the class table. Each imprint is a skill or tool proficiency taken from a previous life; you are proficient in all of them, and you can swap one imprint for another whenever you finish a long rest, as an old life surfaces."},{"type":"p","text":"Imprints do not feel like your own knowledge. They arrive as reflex \u2014 hands that know a weapon you have never fired, a language you have never studied answering itself in your mouth."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Stack Protocol","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Revenant or Archivist. Your protocol grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20 (22 where a sleeve package raises it). You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Needlecast","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can transmit yourself. As an action, spend 1 Stack Charge to cast your consciousness to any prepared sleeve, empty body or compatible construct within the range shown on the class table. Your old body drops, empty and alive but vacant, and you arrive instantly."},{"type":"p","text":"You have a pool of Stack Charge shown on the class table, regained on a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Past Lives","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per short rest, you can reach for a life that knew how to handle this. You gain proficiency \u2014 or expertise, if already proficient \u2014 in one skill of your choice for 10 minutes, and can add your Stackborn level to a single check made with it during that time."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Resleeve","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your return is faster and cheaper: resleeving takes 1 hour rather than 24 and costs 5,000\u20b5. You can also take a sleeve that is not prepared for you \u2014 a fresh corpse, a vat body, an unoccupied clone \u2014 with no penalty beyond the DM's opinion of where you found it."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ghostwalk","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For up to 10 minutes, spending 1 Stack Charge, you can exist without a body: pure signal moving through any connected system, unable to affect the physical world but able to observe it through any sensor, screen or microphone. Nothing can perceive you but a Wirewalker running hot."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Backup","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You keep a copy. Once per week you can commit a backup of yourself to secure storage. If both your body and your stack are destroyed, you return from the backup in a new sleeve after 1d4 days."},{"type":"p","text":"You return as of the moment the backup was taken. Everything since then \u2014 the job, the argument, the person you met last week \u2014 is gone, and the table should play that as it lands."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Two Places at Once","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can spend 3 Stack Charge to run a second instance of yourself in another sleeve for 1 hour. Both are you; both act on your initiative with full ability; both share your memories up to the split."},{"type":"p","text":"At the end of the hour the copies must merge or one must be destroyed. This is double sleeving, it is illegal essentially everywhere, and the penalty for it is usually the erasure of the stack rather than a court appearance."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Stack Hardening","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your stack's AC becomes 24 and its hit points 40, and it is immune to damage that does not specifically target it. You also become aware, instantly, of any attempt to access, copy or locate your backup."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Real Death","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have been through enough bodies to stop treating any of them as load-bearing. When your sleeve is destroyed, you can immediately needlecast to any sleeve within range as a reaction, with no charge cost, arriving with half your hit point maximum."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, you can no longer be permanently killed except by destroying every stack and every backup of you in existence, simultaneously. Any enemy who wants you gone has to make it a project."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["stackborn-revenant","stackborn-archivist"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"},{"name":"Bioforged","hit":"d10","primary":["Con"],"saves":["Str","Wis"],"skillCount":2,"skills":["Athletics","Intimidation","Medicine","Nature","Perception","Stealth","Survival"],"armor":"Light armor, medium armor","weapons":"Simple weapons, martial weapons","firearms":"All simple firearms","tools":"Herbalism kit","resource":"Biomass","tagline":"Grew the upgrade instead of bolting it on, and something is still growing.","description":["Chrome is an admission that the body failed. The Bioforged reject the premise. Their augmentation is cultured, not manufactured \u2014 tissue grown in a vat and coaxed into the host, a second heart, a nictitating membrane, muscle that contracts harder than muscle should. Nothing about them sets off a metal detector.","This is the expensive road. Grown ware costs more, takes longer, and requires a practitioner who is part surgeon and part gardener. What it buys is a body that still reads as a body: no Humanity cost, no cyberpsychosis, no dead-eyed drift. The price is paid on a different ledger entirely.","That ledger is Essence \u2014 the coherence of the organism you started as. Chrome hollows out the person. Grafts crowd out the species. A Bioforged who goes far enough does not lose their humanity so much as stop being the animal they were born as, and the last stretch of that road is not reversible."],"progression":{"type":"table","title":"Class Progression","headers":["Level","Prof.","Features","Biomass","Grafts","Essence"],"rows":[["1st","+2","Grafts, Essence","2","2","20"],["2nd","+2","Adaptive Physiology","3","2","20"],["3rd","+2","Strain","3","3","19"],["4th","+2","Ability Score Improvement","4","3","19"],["5th","+3","Extra Attack","5","4","18"],["6th","+3","Strain feature","5","4","18"],["7th","+3","Regenerative Tissue","6","5","17"],["8th","+3","Ability Score Improvement","7","5","17"],["9th","+4","Second Heart","7","6","16"],["10th","+4","Strain feature","8","6","16"],["11th","+4","Rapid Mutation","9","7","15"],["12th","+4","Ability Score Improvement","9","7","15"],["13th","+5","Hyper-Adaptation","10","8","14"],["14th","+5","Strain feature","11","8","14"],["15th","+5","Immune Ascendancy","11","9","13"],["16th","+5","Ability Score Improvement","12","9","13"],["17th","+6","Strain feature","13","10","12"],["18th","+6","Apex Biology","13","10","12"],["19th","+6","Ability Score Improvement","14","11","11"],["20th","+6","Speciation","15","12","10"]]},"features":[{"name":"Grafts","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You carry cultured tissue rather than hardware. You know a number of grafts shown on the class table, chosen from the graft list below. Grafts are always active. Growing a new graft takes 8 hours of rest and a herbalism kit; you can replace one graft with another whenever you gain a level in this class."},{"type":"table","title":"Graft List","headers":["Graft","Effect"],"rows":[["Dermal Weave","Your AC equals 13 + your Dexterity modifier while unarmoured."],["Reinforced Frame","Your carrying capacity doubles and you have advantage on Strength saving throws."],["Spur Claws","Your unarmed strikes deal 1d8 slashing damage and count as martial weapons."],["Filter Lungs","You are immune to inhaled poison, tear gas and airborne disease, and can breathe anywhere with atmosphere."],["Tapetum","You have darkvision out to 120 feet and advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks relying on sight."],["Adrenal Gland","Once per short rest you can take an additional action on your turn as a bonus action."],["Clotting Factor","You stabilise automatically at 0 hit points and cannot be made to bleed."],["Gecko Pads","You have a climbing speed equal to your walking speed and can climb any surface."],["Lateral Line","You have blindsight out to 30 feet and cannot be surprised by a creature that is touching the ground."],["Toxin Sac","Your natural weapons deal an extra 1d6 poison damage, and a creature you hit must succeed on a Constitution save against your Graft DC or be poisoned until the end of your next turn."],["Stored Fat","You can go a month without food or water, and you have resistance to cold damage."],["Second Stomach","You can eat anything organic, including things that would poison a person, and regain 1d8 hit points when you do."]]},{"type":"p","text":"Your Graft DC is 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Essence","level":1,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Grafts cost nothing on the Humanity track \u2014 nothing about you reads as artificial. They cost Essence instead, the coherence of the organism you started as. Your Essence is shown on the class table and falls as your body accumulates tissue that was never meant to be part of it."},{"type":"table","title":"Essence","headers":["Essence","State","Effect"],"rows":[["15 or more","Baseline","You read as an ordinary member of your species."],["11\u201314","Divergent","Medical scanners flag you as anomalous. You have advantage on saving throws against poison and disease, and disadvantage on Charisma checks with anyone who has seen your medical file."],["6\u201310","Unclassified","Healing you receive from another creature's abilities is halved \u2014 your biology no longer matches the textbook. You gain a natural weapon dealing 1d10 damage of a type you choose when you reach this state."],["1\u20135","Post-Human","You no longer register as a humanoid to any effect that targets creature type. You have resistance to one damage type of your choice, and you require a specialist to treat you at all."],["0","Speciated","You are no longer what you were. Without the 20th-level Speciation feature, your character becomes an NPC \u2014 something the party may still recognise, and may not."]]},{"type":"p","text":"Essence can be recovered by having grafts surgically removed: 1 Essence per graft, over a week of recovery, at a cost of 20,000\u20b5 and the loss of the graft."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Adaptive Physiology","level":2,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your body reorganises to suit the problem. You have a pool of Biomass shown on the class table, regained on a long rest. As a bonus action you can spend it:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Harden (1). You gain resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage until the start of your next turn.","Surge (1). Your speed doubles and you gain a climbing speed until the end of your turn.","Knit (1). You regain hit points equal to 1d10 + your Constitution modifier.","Sharpen (2). Your natural weapons deal an extra 2d6 damage until the end of your turn.","Shed (2). You end one condition affecting you, or escape one grapple or restraint automatically, by leaving part of yourself behind."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Strain","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose Chimeric or Symbiont. Your strain grants features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, 14th and 17th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","level":4,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can increase one ability score by 2, or two ability scores by 1 each, to a maximum of 20. You gain this feature again at 8th, 12th, 16th and 19th level."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Extra Attack","level":5,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can attack twice, rather than once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Regenerative Tissue","level":7,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You regain hit points equal to your Constitution modifier at the start of each of your turns, provided you have at least 1 hit point. Over a long rest you regrow lost limbs and organs."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Second Heart","level":9,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A redundant organ takes over when the first fails. When you are reduced to 0 hit points, you can choose to drop to 1 instead. Once per long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"You also have advantage on Constitution saving throws and cannot be reduced below half your hit point maximum by poison damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Rapid Mutation","level":11,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can swap one graft for another from the list, taking effect immediately. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest \u2014 the body simply reconfigures, painfully and wetly."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hyper-Adaptation","level":13,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The first time each combat you take damage of a given type, you gain resistance to that damage type for the rest of the encounter."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Immune Ascendancy","level":15,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You are immune to poison and disease, cannot be paralysed or put to sleep, and automatically succeed on saving throws against any effect that would alter your form against your will."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Apex Biology","level":18,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Constitution score increases by 4, to a maximum of 24. Your natural weapons deal an extra die of damage, and your Regenerative Tissue restores hit points equal to twice your Constitution modifier."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Speciation","level":20,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You reach the end of the road deliberately rather than by accident. Your Essence can fall to 0 without you being lost: instead, you complete the transition into something new."},{"type":"p","text":"You know every graft on the list simultaneously. Your creature type changes to monstrosity, you no longer age, and you gain a flying or swimming speed equal to your walking speed, chosen when you speciate."},{"type":"p","text":"You are also, now, a founder. Whether the thing you have become can have children, and what they would be, is the finest campaign hook this expansion contains, and it is handed to the DM without further comment."}],"sub":false}],"subclassIds":["bioforged-chimeric","bioforged-symbiont"],"subclassLevel":3,"origin":"expansion"}],"subclasses":[{"id":"wirewalker-icebreaker","cls":"Wirewalker","name":"Icebreaker","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Goes through the defences rather than around them.","description":["Some runners treat ICE as weather to be avoided. The Icebreaker treats it as a door with a lock on it, and carries a very large key. This is the loud school of intrusion \u2014 fast, direct, and entirely dependent on being finished before the response team arrives.","It is also the school that gets hired when the job is not theft but demolition: when a client wants a network to stop existing and does not much care who knows."],"features":[{"name":"Assault Deck","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with martial firearms, and you know the Icepick program without it counting against your programs known. When you run Icepick, it deals an extra 1d8 damage."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, when you reduce a piece of ICE to 0 hit points you regain Bandwidth equal to your proficiency bonus."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Breach","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you enter a new floor of an architecture, you can immediately make one Interface attack against a construct on it as part of the same action."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Feedback Loop","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a piece of ICE damages you, you can use your reaction to reflect it. The ICE takes damage equal to the damage you took, and any creature monitoring that ICE takes half as much psychic damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Shatterpoint","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Interface attacks score a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20 against constructs, and a critical hit from an Interface attack disables the target for 1 minute in addition to its damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Total War","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can declare an architecture hostile. Every piece of ICE in it takes 10d10 damage and must succeed on a saving throw against your Interface DC or be destroyed outright. The architecture itself is crippled for 24 hours and its owner will know, within the hour, exactly what grade of professional did this."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"wirewalker-wraith-protocol","cls":"Wirewalker","name":"Wraith Protocol","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Was never there, and has the absence of logs to prove it.","description":["The Wraith's ambition is to be an absence. No alarm, no trace, no anomalous power draw, no security officer waking at 4am with the sense that something is wrong with the building. A run that ends with anyone knowing a run happened is, by this school's standards, a failure regardless of what you came out holding.","Wraiths are the most expensive runners on the market and the hardest to find, for reasons that ought to be obvious."],"features":[{"name":"Null Signature","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know the Wraith program without it counting against your programs known, and its Bandwidth cost is halved for you."},{"type":"p","text":"While you are inside an architecture, ICE must succeed on a check against your Interface DC to perceive you at all. ICE that cannot perceive you cannot act against you."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Sidestep","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a construct would detect you or an attack would hit you inside an architecture, you can use your reaction to dump 3 Bandwidth and be somewhere else \u2014 the detection fails, the attack misses, and you move to any node on your current floor."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Borrowed Face","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can spend 1 minute and 4 Bandwidth to become, as far as a system is concerned, someone who belongs there. You gain the credentials, clearance and access history of any person whose records the architecture holds, for 1 hour. Their logs will show them doing everything you do."}],"sub":false},{"name":"No Such Event","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can edit a system's memory of the last hour: alarms un-ring, footage shows an empty corridor, and any creature that witnessed you through that system's sensors must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your Interface DC or become convinced it saw nothing."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Nobody","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have been erased so thoroughly and so often that reality has started cooperating. Automated systems \u2014 cameras, turrets, drones, biometric locks, tracking software \u2014 cannot perceive you unless you allow it. You do not appear in recordings. You cannot be the target of a scrying sensor, a trace, or any divination that works through technology."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"puppeteer-swarm-handler","cls":"Puppeteer","name":"Swarm Handler","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"A hundred small problems arriving at once.","description":["Big frames get shot at. Small frames get ignored until there are sixty of them in the room and the exits are welded. The Swarm Handler builds down rather than up: palm-sized rotors, insect crawlers, things that fit through a ventilation grille and reassemble on the other side.","Handlers are the reason serious facilities filter their air."],"features":[{"name":"Motes","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain a swarm of motes \u2014 a cloud of palm-sized drones that occupies a 5-foot space, moves 30 feet (fly, hover), has AC 14 and hit points equal to five times your Puppeteer level, and is treated as one frame."},{"type":"p","text":"The swarm can occupy another creature's space. As an action while you control it, it deals 2d6 slashing damage to every creature in its space, increasing to 3d6 at 10th level and 4d6 at 17th."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Saturation","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your swarm imposes disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks made by any creature sharing its space, and creatures inside it cannot benefit from half cover or three-quarters cover."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Reassemble","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When your swarm is destroyed, it re-forms at the start of your next turn with half its hit points, as long as any part of it remains. You can do this once per short rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Divide","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can split the swarm into two independent swarms, each with half the original's current hit points, as a bonus action. They can be merged again the same way."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Grey Tide","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your swarm can now fill a 20-foot cube. Once per long rest you can command it to consume: every object and creature in its space takes 8d6 slashing damage, non-magical objects up to Large size are reduced to component parts, and the swarm heals to full from the material."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"puppeteer-panzer-jockey","cls":"Puppeteer","name":"Panzer Jockey","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"One frame, enormous, and a deep reluctance to leave it.","description":["The other doctrine builds a fleet. The Panzer Jockey builds a home. One chassis, over-armoured and over-gunned, rebuilt after every job and never quite finished \u2014 a rolling argument that the correct response to a hostile city is a heavier vehicle.","Jockeys tend to name the frame, talk to it, and take its damage personally."],"features":[{"name":"Heavy Chassis","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your frame is Large, its tier is treated as one higher for hit points and armour class, and it gains proficiency with all firearms, including mounted weapons. You can mount one firearm on it, which it fires using your Intelligence modifier for attack and damage."},{"type":"p","text":"The frame's speed is reduced by 10 feet and it cannot fit through a space narrower than 5 feet."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Reactive Plating","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"While jumped in, when the frame takes damage you can use your reaction to reduce it by 1d10 + your Puppeteer level. If the damage is reduced to 0, the attacker takes 2d6 fire damage from the venting plate."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Weapons Free","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can mount a second firearm, and when you take the Attack action while jumped in you can fire both as part of that action. Attacking at long range imposes no disadvantage for either."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Unstoppable","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your frame ignores difficult terrain, cannot be knocked prone, restrained or grappled, and can move through walls of wood, plaster or glass, reducing them to rubble as it passes."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Fortress","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The frame becomes cover. Allies within 10 feet of it have half cover, and while you are jumped in it is immune to critical hits and has resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, when the frame would be destroyed, it instead sheds its outer armour in a 20-foot radius \u2014 every creature there takes 6d10 bludgeoning damage \u2014 and continues at half its hit point maximum."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"chromehound-reflex-arsenal","cls":"Chromehound","name":"Reflex Arsenal","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Draws faster than the eye resolves, and does it four times.","description":["The Reflex Arsenal school buys speed and spends it on volume. Wired reflexes, smartlinked everything, a weapon in each hand and two more within reach. In a firefight the Arsenal operator is the one who has already acted twice while everyone else is still deciding to.","The tradeoff is structural: there is no armour in this build, only the theory that nothing gets to shoot back."],"features":[{"name":"Wired","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your speed increases by 10 feet and you can take the Dash or Disengage action as a bonus action."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, you can draw or stow any number of weapons whenever you could normally draw or stow one, and drawing a weapon does not end your turn's movement."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Double Tap","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you take the Attack action with a one-handed firearm, you can make one additional attack with a different one-handed firearm you are holding as a bonus action, and you add your ability modifier to its damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Preemption","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature within 30 feet of you takes an action, you can use your reaction to make one weapon attack against it before its action resolves. If that attack reduces it to 0 hit points, its action is lost."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Blur","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Attack rolls against you have disadvantage while you are not incapacitated and are wearing no armour heavier than light armour."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Trigger Discipline","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once on each of your turns when you score a critical hit or reduce a creature to 0 hit points, you can immediately take another full Attack action."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"chromehound-bulwark-protocol","cls":"Chromehound","name":"Bulwark Protocol","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Stands where the shooting is and refuses to be a casualty.","description":["Bulwark operators are bought by people who need to arrive somewhere alive. The build is subdermal plate, structural reinforcement and a reworked pain response \u2014 a body optimised not for output but for continuing to exist in conditions where existing is the hard part.","They are the closest thing the street has to a knight, and they know it, and most of them find the comparison embarrassing and accurate."],"features":[{"name":"Subdermal Plate","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"While you are wearing no armour or light armour, your AC equals 13 + your Constitution modifier + your Dexterity modifier (maximum +2). This stacks with a shield."},{"type":"p","text":"You also gain proficiency with heavy weapons and can ignore the massive property on firearms."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Interpose","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a creature you can see attacks a target within 5 feet of you, you can use your reaction to become the target instead. The attack is made against you, and you have resistance to its damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Ablative Systems","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"At the start of each of your turns in combat you gain temporary hit points equal to your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier, which last until the start of your next turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Immovable","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You cannot be moved against your will, knocked prone, or teleported by an unwilling effect. Difficult terrain costs you no extra movement, and you have advantage on saving throws against effects that would incapacitate you."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Bunker","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You and every ally within 10 feet of you have resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage from ranged attacks."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as a reaction to taking damage, you can lock down: until the start of your next turn, you and every ally within 10 feet take no damage from any source."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"streetdoc-ripperdoc","cls":"Streetdoc","name":"Ripperdoc","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Installs chrome anywhere, including mid-firefight.","description":["The Ripperdoc's speciality is the surgery that should not be attempted outside an operating theatre, performed outside an operating theatre, usually at speed. They keep a catalogue in their head and a case of ware in the boot, and their waiting room is whatever hallway you bled into.","Their clients love them, distrust them, and come back, because nobody else will fit a cyberlimb in ninety minutes with no questions and no records."],"features":[{"name":"Back-Alley Clinic","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can install cyberware or augments over a short rest, anywhere, without a clinic. The surgery fee for anything you install is halved."},{"type":"p","text":"You also gain proficiency with tinker's tools and electrician's tools if you don't have it, and can identify any implant a creature carries on sight."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Field Fitting","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action you can install a single tier 1 implant into a willing creature in combat. It functions immediately. The creature takes 2d6 necrotic damage and loses Humanity as normal."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Chop Shop","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can salvage installed ware from a creature that is dead, unconscious or willing, recovering it intact in 10 minutes. Salvaged ware can be resold at half value or installed as normal."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Tuned Install","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Ware you install performs beyond specification. A creature carrying an implant you personally installed adds your proficiency bonus to one ability check or saving throw of its choice per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Rebuild","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, over 1 hour, you can rebuild a willing creature. It gains your choice of two tier 3 implants at no credit cost and no Humanity cost, replacing existing ware if needed, and regains all hit points and Hit Dice."},{"type":"p","text":"The creature is incapacitated for the hour and for 1 hour afterwards, which means you had better not be doing this anywhere interesting."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"streetdoc-trauma-team","cls":"Streetdoc","name":"Trauma Team","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Arrives fast, extracts under fire, bills later.","description":["Somewhere between an ambulance service and a private army sits the response contract: a subscriber goes critical, a team drops on the roof, and the client is in surgery inside four minutes regardless of who is shooting at whom. Doctors who came up through that work never really leave the tempo behind.","They are conditioned to go toward the gunfire, which makes them extraordinary in a crisis and difficult to insure."],"features":[{"name":"Response Protocol","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with medium armor and martial firearms."},{"type":"p","text":"When an ally within 60 feet drops to 0 hit points or is reduced below half their hit point maximum, you can use your reaction to move up to your speed toward them without provoking opportunity attacks."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Under Fire","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can administer an ampule, use your Trauma Kit or stabilise a creature without provoking opportunity attacks, and doing so does not break your concentration or your cover."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Extraction","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action you can grab an ally within 5 feet and move up to your speed, carrying them, then spend Trauma Dice on them as part of the same action. The ally's movement is not spent."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Golden Hour","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can declare a golden hour. For the next minute, every ally within 60 feet of you that drops to 0 hit points is stabilised automatically at the start of their next turn, and no ally within 60 feet can die from hit point damage."}],"sub":false},{"name":"No One Left","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your Combat Triage reaction has no limit on its uses, and when you use it the ally regains hit points equal to the die roll plus your Streetdoc level instead of 1 plus the roll."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, allies you have treated within the last hour who die can be revived by your Crash Cart feature for up to 10 minutes after death rather than 1."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"fixer-broker","cls":"Fixer","name":"Broker","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"If it can be bought, stolen or fabricated, it is already on its way.","description":["The Broker's discipline is logistics. Not people \u2014 goods. Where the shipment is, who is short this month, which warehouse has a night manager with debts, what a prototype is worth before anyone official knows it exists.","A Broker treats the crew as a supply problem to be solved, and is usually offended by how badly they treat the equipment."],"features":[{"name":"The Catalogue","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can acquire any item from this book's equipment, cyberware or augment lists at half price, given 24 hours and a legal or illegal channel."},{"type":"p","text":"You also start each job with a stash: choose items from the equipment chapter worth up to 1,000\u20b5 times your Fixer level, held in caches around the city. Retrieving one takes an hour."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Quartermaster","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you spend a Favour die on Call It In, the value ceiling is doubled and the delivery arrives in 10 minutes rather than an hour."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Grey Import","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can procure things that are not supposed to exist on this market: military hardware, prototype ware, restricted chems. Such items cost triple and require a Favour die, but they are obtainable, and nobody asks."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Depreciation","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Equipment you supply to allies performs above grade. An ally using a weapon, armour or vehicle you personally sourced adds your proficiency bonus to one attack roll, damage roll or saving throw made with it per short rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Arms Dealer","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, over 10 minutes, you can outfit the entire party for a specific job: every ally gains one item of your choice from the equipment, cyberware or augment lists worth up to 50,000\u20b5, on loan, for the duration."},{"type":"p","text":"What is not returned comes out of everyone's cut."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"fixer-handler","cls":"Fixer","name":"Handler","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Runs people the way other Fixers run product.","description":["Handlers deal in the only asset that thinks for itself. They recruit, they place, they maintain \u2014 an informant inside a corp tower, a cousin on a loading dock, a bored security officer who now checks a particular camera less often than she should.","The good ones are genuinely liked by their assets, which is both the tradecraft and the thing that eventually breaks them."],"features":[{"name":"Assets","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Two of your contacts become assets: they are placed somewhere useful and will take real risks for you. You gain one additional asset at 10th and 17th level."},{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, you can activate an asset to accomplish one off-screen task within their reach \u2014 unlocking a door, deleting a record, delaying a patrol, getting a package inside. It works, though not always cleanly."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Read the Room","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can use a bonus action to study a creature you can see. You learn its greatest current fear, its greatest current want, and whether it is currently lying to you."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Recruiter","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, you can attempt to turn a hostile humanoid that can hear and understand you. It makes a Wisdom saving throw against your Fixer DC (8 + proficiency + Charisma). On a failure it is charmed for 10 minutes and treats you as a trusted employer; if the encounter ends without it being harmed by your side, it may become a contact. Once per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Deniability","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When a plan involving one of your assets fails, it fails away from you. You cannot be implicated, traced or identified as the source, and any creature attempting to do so believes it has found someone else instead."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Everyone Is Somebody's","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, you can reveal that a creature you are facing is, or can immediately be made, one of yours. The creature makes a Charisma saving throw against your Fixer DC. On a failure it will not act against you or your allies for 1 hour, and will provide one piece of true, useful information about its employer."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"firebrand-agitator","cls":"Firebrand","name":"Agitator","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Arrives with a grievance and leaves with a mob.","description":["The Agitator works the physical crowd \u2014 the picket, the queue, the square, the transit platform at the end of a bad shift. They are organisers before they are performers, and what they build does not need them present to keep going, which is the whole point and also how they keep getting away.","Corporate security profiles them as force multipliers, which is exactly correct and deeply unflattering to everyone involved."],"features":[{"name":"Rabble","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Wherever people are gathered, you can raise a mob. As an action, up to ten bystanders within your Audience range make Wisdom saves against your Signal DC; those that fail join you for 10 minutes as a crowd."},{"type":"p","text":"A crowd occupies a 20-foot square, moves 20 feet on your turn, and any hostile creature inside it has disadvantage on attack rolls and treats the area as difficult terrain."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Human Shield","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"While you are within a crowd, ranged attacks against you have disadvantage and you have half cover. You can move through a crowd's space freely."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Escalation","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your crowd can act. As a bonus action you can order it to surge: every hostile creature in its space takes bludgeoning damage equal to twice your Inspiration die and must succeed on a Strength save against your Signal DC or be knocked prone and moved 10 feet."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Contagion","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Creatures that flee, are charmed, or are knocked prone by your features spread it. One additional creature within 10 feet of them must make the same save."}],"sub":false},{"name":"General Strike","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can call a stoppage. For the next hour, in a district of the city, the ordinary machinery of life halts: transit stops, shutters come down, shifts walk out, and the authorities are fully occupied."},{"type":"p","text":"Within that district, hostile reinforcements do not arrive, surveillance is overwhelmed, and every check you or your allies make to move unseen through public space succeeds."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"firebrand-pirate-signal","cls":"Firebrand","name":"Pirate Signal","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Owns a frequency they were never licensed for.","description":["Pirate Signal broadcasts. From a van, a rooftop rig, a hijacked corporate tower \u2014 wherever the aerial goes up, the show goes out, and for as long as it is on air the audience is everyone within range of a screen.","They are the closest thing this setting has to a free press, which mostly means they are the closest thing it has to a wanted list."],"features":[{"name":"On Air","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have a transmitter rig. While broadcasting, your Audience range extends to everyone within 1 mile who is near any active screen, speaker or comm \u2014 whether or not they can see or hear you directly."},{"type":"p","text":"You gain proficiency with hacking tools and electrician's tools, and can use Charisma instead of Intelligence for checks made to work a broadcast or comms system."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Signal Jam","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action you can flood local spectrum. For 1 minute, within 300 feet, all hostile comms, drone control, smartlinks and remote sensors fail, and creatures relying on them have disadvantage on attack rolls. Allies you choose are unaffected."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Deepfake","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can fabricate a broadcast of a real person saying or doing something they did not. Creatures who see it must succeed on an Intelligence saving throw against your Signal DC or believe it; disproving it takes a week and a resourced investigation, by which point it has done its work."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Untraceable","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your broadcasts cannot be located, jammed or taken off air by anything short of physically destroying your rig, and you always know when someone is trying."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Emergency Broadcast","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest you can seize every channel in the city for 1 minute. During it you can be seen and heard by everyone, you know you are being listened to, and any Signal option you use can target any number of creatures in the city."},{"type":"p","text":"Afterwards, everyone who matters knows it was you."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"stackborn-revenant","cls":"Stackborn","name":"Revenant","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Keeps coming back, and keeps a list.","description":["Some Stackborn treat resleeving as a medical procedure. The Revenant treats it as a tactical reset. They have died more than most and take it worse each time \u2014 not afraid, exactly, but accumulating. Every sleeve they wear is built around finishing something the last one started.","They are extremely hard to discourage, which is the polite way of saying they are difficult to be in a party with."],"features":[{"name":"Death Debt","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you take a new sleeve after dying, mark the creature or organisation that killed you. You have advantage on attack rolls against them, and deal an extra 1d6 damage to them, until the debt is settled to your satisfaction."},{"type":"p","text":"You can hold one debt at a time, increasing to two at 10th level and three at 17th."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Spite","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you are reduced to 0 hit points, you can use your reaction to make one weapon attack against a creature within reach before you fall."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Rebuilt for This","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Each new sleeve you take comes optimised. You gain a second sleeve package, and its ability score increase stacks with the first."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Terminal Velocity","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"While you are below half your hit point maximum you gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls, and you have resistance to all damage. You do not care what happens to this body, and the body has been informed."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Nothing Sticks","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, when you die, you return immediately in a spare sleeve you have staged nearby, at half hit points, on your next turn. No clinic, no downtime, no 24 hours."},{"type":"p","text":"The people who just killed you find this deeply demoralising, and the DM is encouraged to let them react accordingly."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"stackborn-archivist","cls":"Stackborn","name":"Archivist","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Carries more lives than are strictly theirs.","description":["The Archivist collects. Stacks, imprints, fragments, the recorded last hours of people nobody else kept. Some do it out of scholarship, some out of grief, some because a personality stored in a drawer is the most valuable and most blackmailable object in the city.","An Archivist is never quite alone in their own head, and has mostly made peace with the arrangement."],"features":[{"name":"The Collection","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You carry a small case of recorded personalities. Your imprints double, and you can swap any imprint as a bonus action rather than on a long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"You can also consult the collection: once per short rest, ask the DM one question about a place, organisation or person that existed within the last century, and receive a true if incomplete answer from someone who was there."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Borrowed Hands","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"When you make an attack roll, ability check or saving throw, you can call up a specialist from the collection and add your Charisma modifier to the result. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Read the Stack","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You can interface with a cortical stack \u2014 including one taken from a corpse \u2014 over 10 minutes, and experience its owner's final hour in full. You learn what they knew, what killed them, and one secret they were keeping."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Composite","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You blend the collection into yourself. You gain proficiency in all saving throws, and you cannot be charmed, frightened or possessed \u2014 there is no clear single mind in there to take hold of."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Congress","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Once per long rest, as an action, you can convene the collection for 1 minute. During it you have advantage on every ability check and saving throw, you can take two actions on each of your turns, and you cannot be surprised."},{"type":"p","text":"Afterwards you take 6d6 psychic damage, and you spend the next hour unsure which of the opinions in your head is yours."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"bioforged-chimeric","cls":"Bioforged","name":"Chimeric","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Borrowed the best parts of six species and kept going.","description":["The Chimeric strain treats the animal kingdom as a parts catalogue. Cat's eyes, mantis forelimbs, the pressure tolerance of something that lives at depth \u2014 grafted in, tuned, and held together by a great deal of expensive immunosuppression.","Chimerics are visibly not standard. Most stop trying to pass fairly early, and a few find the freedom in that genuinely liberating."],"features":[{"name":"Beast Grafts","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain two additional grafts, and they do not reduce your Essence."},{"type":"p","text":"Your natural weapons count as magical for the purpose of overcoming resistance and immunity."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Predator's Read","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You gain advantage on Wisdom (Perception) and Wisdom (Survival) checks relying on smell or hearing, and you can track a creature by scent for up to 24 hours after it passed."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Pounce","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"If you move at least 20 feet in a straight line toward a creature and hit it with a natural weapon on the same turn, it must succeed on a Strength saving throw against your Graft DC or be knocked prone. If it is prone, you can make one additional attack against it as a bonus action."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Hybrid Vigour","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose two damage types. You have resistance to both. Additionally, you can spend 2 Biomass as a reaction to gain immunity to one damage type until the start of your next turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Apex Form","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"As an action, spend 4 Biomass to assume your apex form for 10 minutes. You become Large, your natural weapons deal an extra 2d8 damage, your speed increases by 20 feet, your reach increases by 5 feet, and you have advantage on Strength checks and saving throws."},{"type":"p","text":"While in this form you cannot speak in any language, use firearms, or pass for a person under any circumstances at all."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null},{"id":"bioforged-symbiont","cls":"Bioforged","name":"Symbiont","levelAvailable":3,"tagline":"Is not alone in there, and the other one is helping.","description":["The Symbiont strain does not graft tissue. It hosts an organism \u2014 a cultured partner, grown alongside, seated along the spine and through the chest cavity, with its own reflexes and its own opinions about danger.","Hosts describe the relationship in wildly different terms: a colleague, a pet, a second set of instincts, a passenger who will not stop talking. What they agree on is that it is very good at keeping them alive, and that it wants things."],"features":[{"name":"The Passenger","level":3,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You host a symbiont. It has its own senses and reflexes:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You cannot be surprised, and you have advantage on initiative rolls.","You can see in all directions \u2014 attackers gain no benefit from being unseen or behind you.","As a reaction, the symbiont can make one unarmed strike dealing 1d8 + your Constitution modifier piercing damage against a creature within 10 feet."]}],"sub":false},{"name":"Shared Burden","level":6,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The symbiont takes some of what hits you. When you take damage, you can use your reaction to reduce it by 1d10 + your Bioforged level. Doing so costs 1 Biomass and the symbiont is sluggish until the end of your next turn."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Second Opinion","level":10,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your symbiont notices what you miss. When you fail an ability check or saving throw, it can insist: reroll, with advantage. You can do this a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest."},{"type":"p","text":"It is not always right. It is, however, always confident."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Extension","level":14,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The symbiont can leave you for short periods. As an action, it detaches and acts as a separate creature with your Constitution score, AC, half your hit points and a speed of 40 feet, for up to 10 minutes. It acts on your initiative and you can see through its senses. If it dies, you take 6d6 necrotic damage and lose this feature until you finish a long rest."}],"sub":false},{"name":"Two Minds","level":17,"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You and the symbiont act in parallel. You can take two reactions per round rather than one, and once on each of your turns you can take an additional bonus action."},{"type":"p","text":"Additionally, if you are reduced to 0 hit points, the symbiont takes over: you act normally for 1 minute at 0 hit points, at which point you drop unless healed. Once per long rest. What it does with the minute is broadly what you would have done, with fewer reservations."}],"sub":false}],"sidebars":[],"statblocks":[],"origin":"expansion","page":null}],"feats":[{"name":"Chrome Junkie","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have rebuilt yourself past the point most bodies tolerate, and yours keeps accepting the load. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You gain a 15-point Humanity tolerance buffer, spent only after your Humanity reaches zero.","The Humanity cost of any cyberware you install is reduced by 1, to a minimum of 1.","You have advantage on saving throws made to resist the Fraying state's hostility."]}],"prerequisite":"At least one installed cyberware implant"},{"name":"Clean Baseline","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have never let anyone put anything inside you, and it shows in ways people find difficult to name. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Charisma or Wisdom score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You are immune to EMP effects, hacking, and any effect that targets cyberware.","You have advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) and Wisdom (Insight) checks made with a creature that is itself heavily chromed \u2014 they find you restful, and slightly sad."]}],"prerequisite":"No installed cyberware or augments"},{"name":"Icebreaker's Instinct","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have been burned by enough black ICE to feel it coming. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Intelligence score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You gain proficiency with hacking tools, or expertise if you already have it.","When ICE would damage you, you can use your reaction to halve that damage."]}],"prerequisite":"Proficiency with hacking tools"},{"name":"Drone Whisperer","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Machines take instruction from you more readily than they should. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Intelligence score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You can issue a command to any friendly drone or construct as a free action once on each of your turns.","You have advantage on checks made to repair, override or reprogram a drone or vehicle."]}]},{"name":"Street Legend","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"People have heard the story. Some of it is even true. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Charisma score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","Your Street Cred increases by 2.","Once per long rest, you can invoke your reputation to make one hostile creature that recognises you hesitate: it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier) or be frightened of you for 1 minute."]}]},{"name":"Fast Draw","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your hand is moving before the decision reaches your mouth. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Dexterity score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You can draw or stow two firearms whenever you could normally draw or stow one.","When you roll initiative and are not surprised, you can immediately make one attack with a one-handed firearm you are holding or can draw."]}]},{"name":"Neural Firewall","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Something in your head bites back. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Intelligence or Wisdom score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You have advantage on saving throws against effects that would read your mind, control your implants, or force you out of a remote body.","A creature that attempts to hack your cyberware and fails takes psychic damage equal to twice your proficiency bonus."]}]},{"name":"Rated for Trauma","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have been declared dead at least twice and found the paperwork premature. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Constitution score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You have advantage on death saving throws.","When you regain hit points from an ally's ability while at 0 hit points, you regain an additional 1d10."]}]},{"name":"Chem Tolerance","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your liver has opinions and no authority. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Constitution score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You have advantage on saving throws against addiction, and you take no penalty from withdrawal.","The beneficial effects of any drug or ampule last twice as long for you."]}]},{"name":"Second Skin","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You wear armour the way other people wear clothes. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You gain proficiency with medium armor and shields, or heavy armor if you already have both.","Wearing armour imposes no disadvantage on your Dexterity (Stealth) checks.","While wearing armour you have resistance to bludgeoning damage from falls, vehicles and explosions."]}]},{"name":"Wall Runner","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The city is a surface and you treat all of it as floor. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Dexterity score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You have a climbing speed equal to your walking speed.","You can move along vertical surfaces and across liquids on your turn without falling, as long as you end your turn on solid ground.","You take half damage from falls and can reduce fall damage further by the usual means."]}]},{"name":"Corporate Ghost","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Whatever file they pull on you is thin and mostly wrong. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Intelligence or Charisma score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","Biometric and records searches for you return nothing, or return someone else.","You have advantage on Charisma (Deception) checks made to pass as an employee, official or licensed professional, and you always have plausible documentation."]}]},{"name":"Grafted","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You have had cultured tissue seated into you by someone who knew what they were doing. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Constitution score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You gain one graft of your choice from the Bioforged graft list. It costs you no Essence and no Humanity.","You have advantage on saving throws against disease."]}]},{"name":"Stack Tapped","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Somebody fitted you with a cortical stack, and you are still deciding how you feel about it. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["You have a cortical stack, as the Stackborn class feature. If your body dies with the stack intact, you can be resleeved given a clinic, 25,000\u20b5 and 24 hours.","You gain one imprint: a skill or tool proficiency from a life that was not yours.","You have disadvantage on saving throws against effects that target your stack specifically \u2014 it is an off-the-shelf model and everyone knows the model."]}]},{"name":"Crowd Sense","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know what a room is about to do before the room does. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Charisma or Wisdom score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You can never be caught in a stampede, crush or riot against your will, and you always find the exit.","Once per short rest you can redirect a crowd's attention, causing every creature that is not hostile to you within 60 feet to look somewhere of your choosing for 6 seconds."]}]},{"name":"Black Market Contacts","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You know which door to knock on, and what to bring. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Charisma score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You can buy restricted, illegal or military-grade equipment at double its listed price, given 24 hours in any settlement of reasonable size.","You can sell stolen goods at 60% of value rather than the usual pittance, and nobody asks where they came from."]}]},{"name":"Smartlinked","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Your weapons are wired into your optic nerve and they no longer feel like tools. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Dexterity or Intelligence score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","You ignore half cover and three-quarters cover with firearm attacks.","Attacking at long range with a firearm does not impose disadvantage on your attack rolls."]}],"prerequisite":"Proficiency with at least one firearm"},{"name":"Overclocked Metabolism","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"You burn hot, heal fast, and will probably not see forty. You gain the following benefits:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Increase your Constitution or Dexterity score by 1, to a maximum of 20.","Your speed increases by 10 feet.","When you finish a short rest you regain hit points equal to your level without spending Hit Dice. Once per long rest.","You require twice as much food and water as normal, and you age at twice the usual rate."]}]}],"systems":[{"name":"Humanity","tagline":"Every piece of chrome is a piece of you that used to be meat.","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Chrome is not free. The genre this book lives in has always charged for it \u2014 an implant buys you speed, reach or a second set of eyes, and takes back some measure of the person you were. Humanity is the ledger."},{"type":"p","text":"Your Humanity score is your Charisma score multiplied by 5, to a maximum of 100. A character with Charisma 12 starts at 60 Humanity. This is your baseline: the distance between you and the thing that walks out of a back-alley clinic with nothing human left behind its eyes."},{"type":"p","text":"Installing cyberware costs Humanity permanently, by tier. Augments \u2014 the smaller, less invasive grade of ware \u2014 cost 1 each. Removing an implant refunds its full Humanity cost after a week of convalescence, which is why so many operators run light before a job that needs a human touch."},{"type":"table","title":"Humanity Cost by Tier","headers":["Installed Ware","Humanity Cost"],"rows":[["Augment (any)","1"],["Cyberware, tier 1","2"],["Cyberware, tier 2","5"],["Cyberware, tier 3","9"],["Cyberware, tier 4","14"]]},{"type":"p","text":"Your Humanity is measured against your starting score as a percentage, so a naturally warm character has further to fall than a cold one. As it drops you pass through states, and each one takes something from you."},{"type":"table","title":"States of Humanity","headers":["Remaining","State","Effect"],"rows":[["60% or more","Baseline","No effect. You still flinch at the right things."],["40\u201359%","Dissociated","You have disadvantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks against anyone who can see your chrome, and on Wisdom (Insight) checks to read emotion."],["20\u201339%","Fraying","When you take a critical hit or drop to 0 hit points, make a DC 12 Wisdom saving throw. On a failure, until the end of your next turn you must move toward and attack the nearest creature, making no distinction between friend and target."],["1\u201319%","Flatlining","You have disadvantage on Wisdom saving throws. A long rest restores only half your spent Hit Dice, rounded down. You no longer dream."],["0","Cyberpsychosis","Your character is lost. They become an NPC under the DM's control. Only sustained therapy and the removal of ware can bring them back, and the person who returns is not quite the person who left."]]},{"type":"p","text":"Therapy. Between jobs you can commit to treatment: 7 days of downtime and 5,000\u20b5 per day restores 1 Humanity per day, to a maximum of your starting score minus the cost of ware still installed. A Streetdoc with the Counsellor's Licence feature halves the cost and doubles the rate."},{"type":"p","text":"A note for the table. Humanity is a horror dial, not a morality one. It does not measure whether a character is good \u2014 a saint with four limbs of surgical steel is still a saint. It measures how far they have drifted from the baseline their own nervous system expects, and how much that drift costs them when they need to look someone in the eye. Groups who want the chrome without the dread should treat the whole track as optional; nothing else in this expansion breaks without it."}]},{"name":"Street Cred","tagline":"What the city thinks you are, before you open your mouth.","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Street Cred is a shared track that runs from 0 to 10 and answers one question: does the street know your name? It rises when you do something the street can see \u2014 a job that made the feeds, a corp embarrassed in public, a debt paid in front of witnesses \u2014 and falls when you are seen to fold."},{"type":"p","text":"Your Cred is a bonus you can add to a Charisma check made against someone who has heard of you, once per scene. It is also a liability: every point of Cred is a point of description in somebody's file on you."},{"type":"table","title":"Street Cred","headers":["Cred","Standing","What It Buys"],"rows":[["0","Nobody","You get searched at the door."],["1\u20132","Known face","+1 to Charisma checks with fixers and gangs. A fixer will take your call."],["3\u20134","Somebody","+2. You can call in a minor favour once per job without spending a Favour die."],["5\u20136","Name","+3. Doors open. So do files \u2014 corps now run your face on sight."],["7\u20138","Legend","+4. Rivals inherit your enemies. One faction actively wants you dead."],["9\u201310","Myth","+5. Strangers do favours unasked, and the price on your head funds a small army."]]},{"type":"p","text":"The DM awards Cred, usually 1 point per job that ended loudly, and takes it back for a public humiliation. A Fixer or a Firebrand generates it faster than anyone; a Wirewalker who does the job properly generates none at all, which is the point of doing the job properly."}]}],"origins":{"name":"Origins","tagline":"Where you were standing when the world happened to you.","intro":["A background says what you did for money. An origin says what was done to you first. Choose one, or roll a d12. An origin grants one small mechanical perk and a hook the DM can pull on. It stacks with your background \u2014 they answer different questions."],"table":{"type":"table","title":"Origins","headers":["d12","Origin","Perk"],"rows":[["1","Arcology Born","You have never touched unfiltered soil. You know corporate procedure cold: advantage on Intelligence checks to recall how a corporation's internal systems or hierarchies work."],["2","Combat Zone Raised","You grew up where the police stopped going. You can always find a defensible position: once per short rest, take the Dodge action as a bonus action."],["3","Debt Indentured","You were born owing. You start with an extra 5,000\u20b5 of gear and a creditor who knows exactly where you sleep."],["4","Orbital Drop","Raised in low gravity, rebuilt for this one. You ignore difficult terrain caused by rubble, wreckage or low visibility."],["5","Nomad Convoy","The road was the address. You gain proficiency with one type of vehicle and can sleep soundly anywhere that moves."],["6","Lab Product","You have a serial number where a birth certificate should be. You have advantage on saving throws against poison and disease, and someone owns your patent."],["7","Church of the Signal","You were raised to believe the NET is listening. You can always tell when a room is under electronic surveillance with a DC 13 Wisdom (Perception) check."],["8","Corporate Legacy","Your family name still opens one door. Once per job, you can invoke it for access \u2014 and the person you invoke it with reports the contact upward."],["9","Gutter Clinic","You were stitched back together by someone unlicensed. You stabilise at 1 hit point instead of 0 the first time you would drop each long rest."],["10","Ex-Military","Someone trained you properly and then discarded you. You gain proficiency with martial firearms and one set of artisan's tools used for maintenance."],["11","Ghost Identity","Officially you do not exist. Biometric and records searches for you fail, which is useful until you need a bank account, a clinic or a lawyer."],["12","Rebuilt","You died once already and something put you back. You have advantage on death saving throws, and you remember nothing from before the table."]]}}};